' LibraryStore — saved content and continue-watching positions, persisted
' locally, pure logic on a registry seam like SettingsStore/AddonsStore.
'
' A real store is built over an roRegistrySection and Load()s its state on
' construction; tests pass a fake registry (or nothing, which means in-memory
' only). Save() writes the whole library as one registry key. Since the app is
' guest-only nothing syncs — this is the local mirror of the Stremio library.
'
' Persistence is a session-aware registry key: a guest session uses "library"
' and a stremio session uses "stremio_library", so the two sessions never share
' saved content or continue-watching positions. What persists differs by
' session: a guest session saves saved items + continue watching (its data is
' local-only, nothing to fetch anywhere), while a stremio session persists ONLY
' the continue-watching stack — the rest of its library is re-synced from the
' Stremio account in the background on launch and lives in memory for the
' session, so nothing is written to the device needlessly. The registry section
' object is shared; only the key changes.
'
' Ordering is the array itself: freshly written items land at index 0, so the
' newest is always first and no sequence number or sort is needed. Continue
' watching is a capped stack — SetPosition drops the old entry for the same
' video/series, pushes the new one on top, and pops anything beyond the cap.
'
' Membership keeps that stack in step with the library, mirroring Stremio where
' CW is a view over the account library: RemoveSaved drops the meta's entries (a
' removed, non-temp account item is not in CW), and AddSaved re-seeds from the
' account item's progress on stremio — the same state AddToLibrary reuses. A
' guest has no account item to re-seed from, so a guest re-add stays out of CW;
' that divergence is deliberate, since Stremio has no local-only library.
'
' Helpers live as instance methods: Roku scopes user-defined global functions
' per component, so a bare global called from a method that is invoked from
' another component's code would resolve to invalid (call of a non-function).
'
' Watched state is two layers merged at read time:
'   - the local set (m.watched) is display-side only, written by
'     MarkWatchedIfFinished / MarkSeriesDone, persisted with the saved items so
'     it survives reloads. It is never pushed to the account.
'   - the account layer (m.accountWatched) is re-derived on every sync from the
'     libraryItem state (watched bitfield, flaggedWatched/timesWatched flags,
'     timeOffset), memory-only for the session.
' Internally watched is keyed by videoId (a movie's metaId, or a series'
' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}") so grid tiles ask coarsely with a metaId while
' EpisodesScreen asks per episode.

' Guest libraries persist to the device registry, whose size budget is real, so
' the guest saved list is capped: adding beyond MAX_GUEST_SAVED evicts the
' oldest entry (the array is newest-first, so the tail is least recent),
' mirroring the continue-watching cap. A stremio session is memory-only — its
' saved map is re-synced from the account every launch — so it is never capped
' and the account stays the authority on how many items it holds.
const MAX_GUEST_SAVED = 100

' A video counts as watched when the player position has reached ~70% of its
' duration (so a movie/episode finished per Stremio's rule). position/duration
' are milliseconds; the comparison stays on integer math.
const WATCHED_THRESHOLD = 0.7
const MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING = 8

' Tile glyph tokens. The store maps watched state to a token; PosterTile/EpisodeTile
' turn it into an uri ("pkg:/images/" + token + ".png"). Defined once here so a
' rename touches these two lines and the icon assets, not every screen.
const GLYPH_WATCHED = "eye"
const GLYPH_PROGRESS = "clock"

class LibraryStore
    registry as dynamic
    persistenceRegistry as dynamic
    sessionType as string
    accountScope as string
    dirty as boolean
    accountOutbox as object
    saved as object
    savedOrder as object
    positions as object
    stremioLibrary as object
    watched as object
    accountWatched as object
    unwatched as object
    codec as object

    sub new(registry = invalid as dynamic, sessionType = "guest" as string, accountScope = invalid as dynamic)
        m.persistenceRegistry = registry
        m.registry = registry
        m.accountScope = ""
        m.dirty = false
        if GetInterface(accountScope,"ifString") <> invalid then m.accountScope = accountScope
        if sessionType = "stremio" and accountScope = "" then m.registry = invalid
        if m.registry <> invalid and accountScope <> invalid
            m.registry.Delete("stremio_library")
        end if
        m.sessionType = "guest"
        if sessionType = "stremio" then m.sessionType = "stremio"
        m.saved = {}
        m.savedOrder = []
        m.positions = []
        m.stremioLibrary = []
        m.accountOutbox = []
        m.watched = {}
        m.accountWatched = {}
        m.unwatched = {}
        ' Instance the codec here, not inside EpisodeWatched: Roku scopes
        ' user-defined global functions per component, so a bare WatchedCodec()
        ' call from a method invoked under another component's scope resolves to
        ' invalid (attempted call of a non-function). Construction runs under
        ' MainScene scope — MainScene.brs is the only construction site — which
        ' carries WatchedCodec, and the codec's methods only call intrinsics, so
        ' the stored instance is callable from any component.
        m.codec = WatchedCodec()
        m.time = TimeUtil()
        m.videoId = VideoIdCodec()
        m.stremioCodec = StremioLibraryCodec()
        m.Load()
    end sub

    ' A missing AA key reads back as invalid in BrightScript, so this stands in
    ' for roAssociativeArray.DidExist (which the brs interpreter does not
    ' implement).
    function HasKey(aa as object, key as string) as boolean
        if aa = invalid then return false
        return aa[key] <> invalid
    end function

    ' Add a series/movie to the saved library. False when already saved or the
    ' id is blank. A guest library is capped at MAX_GUEST_SAVED — adding past
    ' it drops the oldest entry so the device registry never overflows, exactly
    ' how the continue-watching stack is capped. A stremio session never caps:
    ' its saved map is memory-only and re-synced from the account, so the device
    ' budget does not apply there.
    '
    ' An add also re-seeds the local continue-watching entry from the account
    ' item's stored progress (ReSeedPositionFromAccount): stremio-core's
    ' AddToLibrary reuses the existing library item, so a title that was watched,
    ' added and then removed re-enters CW the moment it is added back. A guest
    ' session has no account item, so nothing is re-seeded and a re-add stays out
    ' of CW.
    function AddSaved(metaId as string, metaType as string, name as string, poster = "" as string, posterShape = "" as string, metadataProviderKey = "" as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" then return false
        if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId) then return false
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            while m.savedOrder.Count() >= MAX_GUEST_SAVED
                oldestId = m.savedOrder.Pop()
                m.saved.Delete(oldestId)
            end while
        end if
        m.saved[metaId] = {
            metaId: metaId
            metaType: metaType
            name: name
            poster: poster
            posterShape: posterShape
            metadataProviderKey: m.SafeProviderKey(metadataProviderKey)
        }
        m.savedOrder.Unshift(metaId)
        m.ReSeedPositionFromAccount(metaId)
        return m.Save()
    end function

    ' Remove a library item and drop its continue-watching entries. Stremio's CW
    ' is a view over the library: a removed (non-temp) item is not in CW, so the
    ' local stack must lose the meta here or the row would stay stale until the
    ' next account sync. Mirrors stremio-core's RemoveFromLibrary (removed:true,
    ' temp:false). A removed-but-watched title keeps its state.timeOffset on the
    ' account, so AddSaved re-seeds it — but only on stremio, since a guest has
    ' no account item to restore from.
    function RemoveSaved(metaId as string) as boolean
        if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId)
            m.saved.Delete(metaId)
            for i = m.savedOrder.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
                if m.savedOrder[i] = metaId then m.savedOrder.Delete(i)
            end for
            m.PrunePositions(metaId)
            m.Save()
            return true
        end if
        return false
    end function

    ' Drop every continue-watching entry for one meta (all episodes of a series).
    ' Membership is what gates CW, and both sessions share this path.
    sub PrunePositions(metaId as string)
        if metaId = "" or m.positions = invalid then return
        for i = m.positions.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            if m.positions[i].metaId = metaId then m.positions.Delete(i)
        end for
    end sub

    ' Rebuild the continue-watching entry an add-to-library should surface, from
    ' the cached account item's own progress — the state stremio-core's
    ' AddToLibrary preserves when it reuses the existing library item
    ' (LibraryItem::from((meta_preview, library_item))). Only stremio has an
    ' account library; a guest returns here without an item and stays out of CW.
    ' A stored-but-untouched item (no progress) seeds nothing, and a live
    ' channel/tv title is never a resume point.
    sub ReSeedPositionFromAccount(metaId as string)
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return
        item = m.FindStremioItem(metaId)
        if item = invalid then return
        parsed = m.stremioCodec.ParseLibraryItem(item)
        if parsed = invalid then return
        if not parsed.inProgress then return
        if m.IsChannelType(parsed.metaType) then return
        m.SetPosition(parsed.videoId, parsed.metaId, parsed.metaType, parsed.season, parsed.episode, parsed.name, parsed.poster, Int(parsed.position / 1000), Int(parsed.duration / 1000), parsed.posterShape)
    end sub

    ' The cached account item for a meta, or invalid when the account library has
    ' never seen it. Reads the committed stremioLibrary (kept current by every
    ' account push), not a server round-trip.
    function FindStremioItem(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" or m.stremioLibrary = invalid then return invalid
        for each item in m.stremioLibrary
            if item <> invalid and Type(item) = "roAssociativeArray" and item._id = metaId then return item
        end for
        return invalid
    end function

    function IsSaved(metaId as string) as boolean
        return m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId)
    end function

    ' Most recently added first — the array holds ids newest-first.
    function SavedItems() as object
        items = []
        for each metaId in m.savedOrder
            if m.HasKey(m.saved, metaId) then items.Push(m.saved[metaId])
        end for
        return items
    end function

    ' The saved list as the Library screen presents it: filtered by content type
    ' and ordered by one of the supported sorts, always a fresh array (the
    ' internal saved map/order are never rearranged — SortByName/SortByWatched
    ' only reorder the returned copy). typeFilter is "all", "movie" or "series";
    ' sort is "recent" (saved order, newest first — the default), "az"/"za"
    ' (case-insensitive by name) or "watched" (any saved item with a
    ' continue-watching position first, most recently watched first — the
    ' positions array is newest-first — then everything else by name). The
    ' Library filter chips only expose All/Movies/Series, so channel/tv entries
    ' cannot be filtered into a view — they remain in the saved set (and account
    ' layer) but never appear in the Library screen grid.
    function LibraryView(typeFilter as string, sort as string) as object
        items = m.SavedItems()
        if typeFilter <> "all"
            filtered = []
            for each item in items
                metaType = item.metaType
                if metaType = invalid then metaType = ""
                if typeFilter = "channel"
                    if metaType = "channel" or metaType = "tv" then filtered.Push(item)
                else
                    if metaType = typeFilter then filtered.Push(item)
                end if
            end for
            items = filtered
        end if
        if sort = "az"
            m.SortByName(items, false)
        else if sort = "za"
            m.SortByName(items, true)
        else if sort = "watched"
            m.SortByWatched(items)
        end if
        return items
    end function

    ' Case-insensitive insertion sort of saved records by name, ascending or
    ' descending. An insertion sort keeps it interpreter-safe, exactly like
    ' SortByMtimeDesc; roArray.Sort with a function comparator is not guaranteed
    ' in the brs interpreter. A malformed (invalid/blank) name is coerced to ""
    ' so the compare cannot throw.
    sub SortByName(items as object, descending as boolean)
        for i = 1 to items.Count() - 1
            temp = items[i]
            j = i
            while j > 0
                left = items[j - 1].name
                if left = invalid then left = ""
                right = temp.name
                if right = invalid then right = ""
                if descending
                    if LCase(left) >= LCase(right) then exit while
                else
                    if LCase(left) <= LCase(right) then exit while
                end if
                items[j] = items[j - 1]
                j = j - 1
            end while
            items[j] = temp
        end for
    end sub

    ' Insertion sort that floats items with a continue-watching position to the
    ' front, most recently watched first (positions is newest-first, so the
    ' earliest array index is the freshest), then the unwatched by name. Any
    ' position under a metaId marks it watched — an episode position counts for
    ' its series.
    sub SortByWatched(items as object)
        rank = {}
        for i = 0 to m.positions.Count() - 1
            mid = m.positions[i].metaId
            if mid <> invalid and mid <> "" and not m.HasKey(rank, mid) then rank[mid] = i
        end for
        for i = 1 to items.Count() - 1
            temp = items[i]
            j = i
            while j > 0
                if not m.WatchedBefore(items[j - 1], temp, rank) then exit while
                items[j] = items[j - 1]
                j = j - 1
            end while
            items[j] = temp
        end for
    end sub

    ' true when a should sort after b in the "watched" sort: a is less recently
    ' watched (higher rank) than b, or equally ranked and names after b. Not
    ' ranked items all share the cap rank, so unwatched sort by name.
    function WatchedBefore(a as object, b as object, rank as object) as boolean
        ra = m.WatchedRank(rank, a.metaId)
        rb = m.WatchedRank(rank, b.metaId)
        if ra <> rb then return ra > rb
        an = a.name
        if an = invalid then an = ""
        bn = b.name
        if bn = invalid then bn = ""
        return LCase(an) > LCase(bn)
    end function

    function WatchedRank(rank as object, metaId as string) as integer
        if metaId <> invalid and metaId <> "" and m.HasKey(rank, metaId) then return rank[metaId]
        return 1000000000
    end function

    ' Live add-ons speak Stremio content types "channel"/"tv". A live stream
    ' never has a resume point, so those entries are kept out of Continue
    ' Watching entirely: here, at the SyncFromStremio mapping, and at the
    ' player's save/publish gates (they share this helper so no caller can
    ' drift). They still ride the saved set and the account layer when the
    ' account has them.
    function IsChannelType(metaType as string) as boolean
        if metaType = "channel" then return true
        if metaType = "tv" then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' Record playback progress for a video (a movie metaId, or the
    ' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}" id for an episode). Drops the previous
    ' entry for the same video or series, pushes the new one on top of the
    ' capped stack, and pops anything beyond MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING. Blank
    ' positions are ignored so a fresh screen never clears stored progress.
    ' Channel/tv playback records nothing — see IsChannelType.
    ' Resume crosses SceneGraph callFunc as one record, avoiding its native
    ' argument limit. The store validates optional fields at the data boundary.
    function SetPositionRecord(packet as dynamic) as boolean
        if Type(packet) <> "roAssociativeArray" then return false
        for each field in ["videoId","metaId","metaType","name","poster","posterShape","metadataProviderKey"]
            if packet[field] = invalid then packet[field] = ""
            if GetInterface(packet[field],"ifString") = invalid then return false
        end for
        if packet.videoId = "" or packet.metaId = "" then return false
        try
            return m.SetPosition(packet.videoId,packet.metaId,packet.metaType,Int(packet.season),Int(packet.episode),packet.name,packet.poster,Int(packet.position),Int(packet.duration),packet.posterShape,packet.metadataProviderKey)
        catch invalidRecord
            return false
        end try
    end function

    function SetPosition(videoId as string, metaId as string, metaType as string, season as integer, episode as integer, name as string, poster = "" as string, position = 0 as integer, duration = 0 as integer, posterShape = "" as string, metadataProviderKey = "" as string) as boolean
        if videoId = "" or metaId = "" then return false
        if m.IsChannelType(metaType) then return false
        metadataProviderKey = m.SafeProviderKey(metadataProviderKey)
        if metadataProviderKey = "" then metadataProviderKey = m.MetadataKeyFor(metaId)
        for i = m.positions.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            if m.positions[i].videoId = videoId or m.positions[i].metaId = metaId
                m.positions.Delete(i)
            end if
        end for
        m.positions.Unshift({
            videoId: videoId
            metaId: metaId
            metaType: metaType
            season: season
            episode: episode
            name: name
            poster: poster
            posterShape: posterShape
            position: position
            duration: duration
            metadataProviderKey: m.SafeProviderKey(metadataProviderKey)
        })
        while m.positions.Count() > MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING
            m.positions.Pop()
        end while
        return m.Save()
    end function

    function Position(videoId as string) as integer
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.videoId = videoId then return entry.position
        end for
        return 0
    end function

    function IsWatching(videoId as string) as boolean
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.videoId = videoId then return true
        end for
        return false
    end function

    ' The continue-watching stack as-is: newest first, already capped. A shallow
    ' copy is returned, never the live m.positions array: callers loop over the
    ' result and may call helpers that themselves scan m.positions, and a nested
    ' for-each over the same roArray on-device stops the outer loop after its
    ' first element (BrightScript shares the array's iterator state).
    function ContinueWatching() as object
        result = []
        for each entry in m.positions
            result.Push(entry)
        end for
        return result
    end function

    ' The most recent continue-watching entry for one series/movie, or invalid
    ' when nothing has been watched. Details uses this to resurrect a resume
    ' hint for episodes opened straight from a catalog row. Since the array is
    ' newest-first, the first match is the one to resume.
    function ResumeFor(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.metaId = metaId then return entry
        end for
        return invalid
    end function

    function RemovePosition(videoId as string) as boolean
        for i = m.positions.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            if m.positions[i].videoId = videoId
                m.positions.Delete(i)
                m.Save()
                return true
            end if
        end for
        return false
    end function

    ' ---- watched state ----

    ' Record that a video finished (position >= duration * WATCHED_THRESHOLD),
    ' when the player knows a duration. Coalesces like SetPosition: the key is
    ' the video id (a movie's metaId, or a series' "{metaId}:{season}:{episode}")
    ' so re-watching never duplicates. The local set is display-side only — it
    ' is written here on both guest and stremio sessions but never pushed to the
    ' account (the push clones the account's own flags, see BuildWatchStateItem).
    sub MarkWatchedIfFinished(metaId as string, videoId as string, position as integer, duration as integer)
        if duration <= 0 then return
        if position < duration * WATCHED_THRESHOLD then return
        key = metaId
        if videoId <> "" then key = videoId
        if key = "" then return
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, key) then return
        m.watched[key] = true
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' Coarse whole-item watched: the local set has the metaId, or the account
    ' layer flagged the whole item watched (flaggedWatched/timesWatched). Movies
    ' answer directly; series tiles should use SeriesStatus for the watched/
    ' progress distinction.
    function IsWatched(metaId as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" then return false
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return true
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account <> invalid and account.watched then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' Per-episode watched, precise. Local set first; when the episode list is
    ' available the account bitfield is decoded against it (it is only an index
    ' into that ordering, so without the list the account part cannot answer).
    ' An account that flagged the whole series watched (no bitfield) counts every
    ' episode — mirroring WatchedSetFor, so badges and what a write would produce
    ' can never disagree. "orderedEpisodes" is the series' ordered video id list.
    function EpisodeWatched(metaId as string, season as integer, episode as integer, orderedEpisodes as object, suppliedVideoId = "" as string) as boolean
        if orderedEpisodes = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodes) <> "roArray" then return false
        videoId = suppliedVideoId
        if videoId = "" then videoId = m.videoId.Build(metaId, season, episode)
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, videoId) then return true
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return true
        if m.IsUnwatchOverridden(metaId, videoId) then return false
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account = invalid then return false
        if account.watched and (account.bitfield = invalid or account.bitfield = "") then return true
        if account.bitfield = invalid or account.bitfield = "" then return false
        if m.codec = invalid then return false
        watched = m.codec.WatchedDecode(account.bitfield, orderedEpisodes)
        if watched <> invalid and m.HasKey(watched, videoId) then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' The watched mark for one regular episode — whether it has aired and, when
    ' aired, whether it is precisely watched. The aired gate exists because an
    ' account bitfield for a series marked fully watched paints the whole known
    ' list, placeholders included, and literally decoding that would put checks
    ' on episodes that don't exist yet. One source for the badge rule shared by
    ' the build and the re-paint, so it cannot drift. `nowIso` is injectable for
    ' tests; production passes the store's TimeUtil stamp.
    function EpisodeMark(metaId as string, season as integer, ep as object, orderedEpisodes as object, nowIso as dynamic) as object
        mark = { aired: false, watched: false }
        if metaId = "" or ep = invalid or ep.episode = invalid then return mark
        if m.time = invalid then return mark
        mark.aired = m.time.EpisodeAired(ep, nowIso)
        if mark.aired
            videoId = ""
            if GetInterface(ep.id, "ifString") <> invalid then videoId = ep.id
            mark.watched = m.EpisodeWatched(metaId, season, ep.episode, orderedEpisodes, videoId)
        end if
        return mark
    end function

    ' Once the full episode list is known, a series whose every regular episode
    ' is watched crosses from in-progress (clock) to done (eye) on the grid
    ' tiles that only carry a coarse SeriesStatus badge. `metaId` is injected so
    ' the completion rule is store-pure and shared by the build and the in-place
    ' re-paint. Persists through MarkSeriesDone on both sessions (display-side).
    sub MarkAllIfDone(metaId as string, anyRegular as boolean, allDone as boolean) as void
        if anyRegular and allDone and metaId <> ""
            m.MarkSeriesDone(metaId)
        end if
    end sub

    ' Coarse series status for grid tiles that have no episode list. "done" when
    ' the whole series is known watched (local MarkSeriesDone, or the account
    ' flagged the series watched); "progress" when some watch state exists —
    ' account in-progress/bitfield, or the local layer (a continue-watching
    ' position or a locally-finished episode); "none" otherwise. Precise done
    ' (every episode) needs the episode list and is EpisodesScreen's job.
    function SeriesStatus(metaId as string) as string
        if metaId = "" then return "none"
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return "done"
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account <> invalid
            if account.watched then return "done"
            if account.inProgress or account.bitfield <> "" then return "progress"
        end if
        ' Guest/local parity: the account layer is the stremio-only source of
        ' in-progress, so a guest's progress can only come from the local layer
        ' (positions + the watched set), mirroring the account's own signals.
        if m.HasLocalSeriesProgress(metaId) then return "progress"
        return "none"
    end function

    ' The local layer's in-progress answer for a series, mirroring the account
    ' layer's inProgress/bitfield: a continue-watching entry with real progress
    ' (position > 0), or a locally-finished episode key ("{metaId}:{season}:
    ' {episode}") that survives even after the CW cap ages the position out.
    ' SeriesStatus gives "done" precedence, so a MarkSeriesDone series never
    ' reads as in progress here.
    function HasLocalSeriesProgress(metaId as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" then return false
        for i = 0 to m.positions.Count() - 1
            if m.positions[i].metaId = metaId and m.positions[i].position > 0 then return true
        end for
        prefix = metaId + ":"
        for each key in m.watched
            if Left(key, prefix.Len()) = prefix then return true
        end for
        return false
    end function

    ' The coarse watched glyph for a grid tile without an episode list. Series
    ' answer by SeriesStatus (done → GLYPH_WATCHED, in-progress → GLYPH_PROGRESS,
    ' untouched → no badge); everything else by IsWatched (GLYPH_WATCHED or none).
    ' One definition here, so renaming a glyph touches the store + the PosterTile
    ' image — not the one-line adapters in Home/Library/Discover/Search.
    function WatchedGlyph(metaId as string, metaType as string) as string
        if metaId = invalid or metaId = "" then return ""
        kind = metaType
        if kind = invalid then kind = ""
        if kind = "series"
            status = m.SeriesStatus(metaId)
            if status = "done" then return GLYPH_WATCHED
            if status = "progress" then return GLYPH_PROGRESS
            return ""
        end if
        if m.IsWatched(metaId) then return GLYPH_WATCHED
        return ""
    end function

    ' The existing continue-watching position for a meta, as the progress bar
    ' needs it (position/duration in ms), or invalid when there is none.
    function ProgressFor(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        for i = 0 to m.positions.Count() - 1
            if m.positions[i].metaId = metaId
                return { position: m.positions[i].position, duration: m.positions[i].duration }
            end if
        end for
        return invalid
    end function

    ' The continue-watching bar fraction for a meta: position/duration clamped to
    ' (0, 1], or invalid when there is no playable progress (never started, bogus
    ' or zero duration). Screen code just paints the returned value — the clamped
    ' fraction math lives here so Home and Library tiles agree on the bar.
    function ProgressFraction(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if metaId = "" then return invalid
        entry = invalid
        for i = 0 to m.positions.Count() - 1
            if m.positions[i].metaId = metaId then entry = m.positions[i]
        end for
        if entry = invalid then return invalid
        if entry.duration = invalid or entry.duration <= 0 then return invalid
        if entry.position = invalid or entry.position <= 0 then return invalid
        fraction = entry.position / entry.duration
        if fraction > 1 then fraction = 1
        return fraction
    end function

    ' Persist a whole-series done flag (guest local, stremio display-only like
    ' the watched set). Used by EpisodesScreen once it has the full episode list
    ' and can see every non-special episode is watched.
    sub MarkSeriesDone(metaId as string)
        if metaId = "" then return
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then return
        m.watched[metaId] = true
        m.Save()
    end sub

    function AccountLayer(metaId as string) as dynamic
        if m.HasKey(m.accountWatched, metaId) then return m.accountWatched[metaId]
        return invalid
    end function

    ' ---- watched edits ----

    ' Mark one regular episode watched in the local display layer and persist.
    ' The whole-series done key is left alone — a single episode mark never turns
    ' a series done (MarkAllIfDone does that once the full list is known and
    ' every tile is watched). Drops any session unwatch override for the episode.
    sub MarkEpisodeWatched(metaId as string, videoId as string) as void
        if metaId = "" or videoId = "" then return
        m.watched[videoId] = true
        m.ClearUnwatchOverride(metaId, videoId)
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' Clear one episode. A local unwatch also drops a previous whole-series done
    ' key — a series with an unwatched episode cannot stay "done". On a stremio
    ' session the unwatch is remembered for the session (m.unwatched), because
    ' the account's bitfield still lists the episode watched until the corrected
    ' bitfield is pushed and re-synced; the override is what keeps both the tile
    ' badge and any re-encoded bitfield honoring "not watched" meanwhile.
    sub MarkEpisodeUnwatched(metaId as string, videoId as string) as void
        if metaId = "" or videoId = "" then return
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, videoId) then m.watched.Delete(videoId)
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then m.watched.Delete(metaId)
        if m.sessionType = "stremio" then m.RecordUnwatchOverride(metaId, videoId)
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' Mark every episode up to and including lastIndex (index into the given
    ' ordered episode id list) watched, in one write. Clears session unwatch
    ' overrides for those ids — they are watched again. The list is whatever
    ' scoped a caller to (the whole series or one season row): the store is
    ' agnostic, the bitfield it later authors stays series-global regardless.
    sub MarkUpToWatched(metaId as string, orderedEpisodeIds as object, lastIndex as integer) as void
        if metaId = "" or orderedEpisodeIds = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodeIds) <> "roArray" or orderedEpisodeIds.Count() = 0 then return
        if lastIndex < 0 then lastIndex = 0
        if lastIndex >= orderedEpisodeIds.Count() then lastIndex = orderedEpisodeIds.Count() - 1
        for i = 0 to lastIndex
            id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
            m.watched[id] = true
            m.ClearUnwatchOverride(metaId, id)
        end for
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' The inverse of MarkUpToWatched: every episode up to and including lastIndex
    ' is cleared locally, the whole-series done key is dropped (a series with an
    ' unwatched episode cannot stay done), and — on a stremio session — the ids
    ' are remembered as unwatch overrides so the badge and any re-encoded
    ' bitfield keep honoring "not watched" until the correction re-syncs.
    sub MarkUpToUnwatched(metaId as string, orderedEpisodeIds as object, lastIndex as integer) as void
        if metaId = "" or orderedEpisodeIds = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodeIds) <> "roArray" or orderedEpisodeIds.Count() = 0 then return
        if lastIndex < 0 then lastIndex = 0
        if lastIndex >= orderedEpisodeIds.Count() then lastIndex = orderedEpisodeIds.Count() - 1
        for i = 0 to lastIndex
            id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
            if m.HasKey(m.watched, id) then m.watched.Delete(id)
            if m.sessionType = "stremio" then m.RecordUnwatchOverride(metaId, id)
        end for
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId) then m.watched.Delete(metaId)
        m.Save()
    end sub

    sub RecordUnwatchOverride(metaId as string, videoId as string) as void
        ov = m.unwatched[metaId]
        if ov = invalid then ov = {} : m.unwatched[metaId] = ov
        ov[videoId] = true
    end sub

    sub ClearUnwatchOverride(metaId as string, videoId as string) as void
        ov = m.unwatched[metaId]
        if ov <> invalid
            if ov[videoId] <> invalid then ov.Delete(videoId)
        end if
    end sub

    ' Whether an episode is under a session unwatch override (a stremio account
    ' still lists it watched until the correction lands and re-syncs).
    function IsUnwatchOverridden(metaId as string, videoId as string) as boolean
        if metaId = "" or videoId = "" then return false
        ov = m.unwatched[metaId]
        if ov <> invalid and ov[videoId] <> invalid then return true
        return false
    end function

    ' The watched set for a series as it must be written to the account: the
    ' local layer (per-episode keys plus the whole-series done key) unioned with
    ' the account's own marks — its bitfield decoded against the ordered list,
    ' or every id when the account flagged the whole series watched without a
    ' bitfield — minus any session unwatch overrides. A written bitfield
    ' replaces state.watched wholesale, so re-encoding only the local layer
    ' would silently wipe the watch marks the account already holds.
    function WatchedSetFor(metaId as string, orderedEpisodeIds as object) as object
        set = {}
        if metaId = "" or orderedEpisodeIds = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodeIds) <> "roArray" then return set
        n = orderedEpisodeIds.Count()
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
            if m.HasKey(m.watched, id) then set[id] = true
        end for
        if m.HasKey(m.watched, metaId)
            for i = 0 to n - 1
                set[orderedEpisodeIds[i]] = true
            end for
        end if
        account = m.AccountLayer(metaId)
        if account <> invalid
            if account.watched and (account.bitfield = invalid or account.bitfield = "")
                for i = 0 to n - 1
                    set[orderedEpisodeIds[i]] = true
                end for
            else if account.bitfield <> invalid and account.bitfield <> ""
                if m.codec <> invalid
                    decoded = m.codec.WatchedDecode(account.bitfield, orderedEpisodeIds)
                    if decoded <> invalid
                        for i = 0 to n - 1
                            id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
                            if decoded[id] <> invalid then set[id] = true
                        end for
                    end if
                end if
            end if
        end if
        ov = m.unwatched[metaId]
        if ov <> invalid
            for i = 0 to n - 1
                id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
                if ov[id] <> invalid then set.Delete(id)
            end for
        end if
        return set
    end function

    ' The id to report as the bitfield's "last watched" slot: the last watched
    ' id in display order, or the caller's current episode when the set has
    ' nothing watched (that slot must never be empty — the decoder refuses it).
    function LastWatchedId(set as object, orderedEpisodeIds as object, videoId as string) as string
        if set = invalid or orderedEpisodeIds = invalid then return videoId
        for i = orderedEpisodeIds.Count() - 1 to 0 step -1
            id = orderedEpisodeIds[i]
            if id <> invalid and set[id] <> invalid then return id
        end for
        if videoId = invalid or videoId = "" then
            if orderedEpisodeIds.Count() > 0 then return orderedEpisodeIds[0]
            return ""
        end if
        return videoId
    end function

    ' Reconcile the store with the account's remote library (from the
    ' datastoreGet pull). The API is the authority, so the whole in-memory state
    ' is rebuilt, never merged: continue watching is re-derived and re-ordered,
    ' the saved map is re-filled, and every item (even non-CW ones) is kept in
    ' stremioLibrary for the future Library screen. Only the continue-watching
    ' stack is written to the device (Save gates it); the rest lives for the
    ' session. Stremio sessions only — a guest store has no library to reconcile
    ' with, and a stray call must never clobber local guest data.
    sub SyncFromStremio(items as dynamic)
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return
        if items = invalid or Type(items) <> "roArray" then return

        m.stremioLibrary = items
        cw = []
        saved = {}
        savedOrder = []
        accountWatched = {}
        for each item in items
            parsed = m.stremioCodec.ParseLibraryItem(item)
            if parsed = invalid then continue for
            ' The account layer: re-derived on every sync, memory-only. It peers
            ' into the item's watch state the same way the app's own watched set
            ' does — flaggedWatched/timesWatched mark a whole item watched,
            ' timeOffset marks it in progress, and the raw watched bitfield is
            ' kept whole so EpisodesScreen can decode it against the episode list.
            accountWatched[parsed.metaId] = {
                watched: parsed.watchedFlag
                inProgress: parsed.inProgress
                bitfield: parsed.bitfield
            }
            if parsed.cw and not m.IsChannelType(parsed.metaType) then cw.Push(parsed)
            if parsed.saved and parsed.metaId <> "" and not m.HasKey(saved, parsed.metaId)
                saved[parsed.metaId] = {
                    metaId: parsed.metaId
                    metaType: parsed.metaType
                    name: parsed.name
                    poster: parsed.poster
                    posterShape: parsed.posterShape
                    metadataProviderKey: m.MetadataKeyFor(parsed.metaId)
                }
                savedOrder.Push(parsed.metaId)
            end if
        end for

        ' Continue watching, newest first. Exactly one resume point survives per
        ' distinct video OR series (mirroring SetPosition's prune), and the stack
        ' is capped at MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING. Tracking seen ids instead of
        ' deleting as we go is what keeps the NEWEST occurrence of each
        ' video/series — a delete-then-push pass over a newest-first array would
        ' leave only the oldest.
        m.stremioCodec.SortByMtimeDesc(cw)
        positions = []
        seenVideo = {}
        seenMeta = {}
        for each entry in cw
            if not m.HasKey(seenMeta, entry.metaId) and not m.HasKey(seenVideo, entry.videoId)
                seenMeta[entry.metaId] = true
                seenVideo[entry.videoId] = true
                positions.Push({
                    videoId: entry.videoId
                    metaId: entry.metaId
                    metaType: entry.metaType
                    season: entry.season
                    episode: entry.episode
                    name: entry.name
                    poster: entry.poster
                    posterShape: entry.posterShape
                    ' The Stremio codec retains raw wire milliseconds; Roku
                    ' resume/history use seconds, including cold-start restores.
                    position: Int(entry.position / 1000)
                    duration: Int(entry.duration / 1000)
                    metadataProviderKey: m.MetadataKeyFor(entry.metaId)
                })
            end if
        end for
        while positions.Count() > MAX_CONTINUE_WATCHING
            positions.Pop()
        end while
        m.positions = positions

        m.saved = saved
        m.savedOrder = savedOrder
        m.accountWatched = accountWatched
        m.Save()
    end sub

    ' The full synced library, kept in memory for the future Library screen.
    function StremioLibraryItems() as object
        return m.stremioLibrary
    end function

    ' Stremio wire-shape parsing and building live in StremioLibraryCodec
    ' (ParseLibraryItem, SortByMtimeDesc, Identity/ResolveLibraryItem and the
    ' three Build*Item writers): pure functions with the session gate, the
    ' freshest-cache read, and the clock injected as parameters. These adapters
    ' keep the public surface MainScene's push sites call through StoreHost —
    ' they refuse guest sessions, stamp `now` when left to default, hand the
    ' store's state to the codec, and then commit the built item back into
    ' stremioLibrary (CommitStremioItem, the update_and_push_items_to_storage
    ' step) so the next push of any kind starts from it.
    function BuildWatchStateItem(packet as dynamic, now = "" as string) as dynamic
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return invalid
        if now = "" then now = m.time.NowIso()
        item = m.stremioCodec.BuildWatchStateItem(m.sessionType, m.stremioLibrary, now, packet)
        m.CommitStremioItem(item)
        return item
    end function

    function BuildLibraryChangeItem(metaId as string, metaType as string, name as string, poster as string, added as boolean, now = "" as string) as dynamic
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return invalid
        if now = "" then now = m.time.NowIso()
        item = m.stremioCodec.BuildLibraryChangeItem(m.sessionType, m.stremioLibrary, now, metaId, metaType, name, poster, added)
        m.CommitStremioItem(item)
        return item
    end function

    ' Build the LibraryItem a watched-mark/unmark push sends. Stremio sessions
    ' only; stamps now when left to default. The bitfield is authored here from
    ' WatchedSetFor (local + account, minus unwatch overrides) so the union
    ' lands, then handed to BuildWatchedItem with the last-watched id. The packet
    ' carries the ordered video ids — the panel's current list, the same one the
    ' account bitfield indexes and the badges are painted from — plus the meta
    ' identity, so a series the account has never seen still lands as a
    ' well-formed entry (which the later add-to-library push then clones).
    function BuildWatchedStateItem(packet as dynamic, now = "" as string) as dynamic
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" then return invalid
        if packet = invalid then return invalid
        metaId = packet.metaId
        if metaId = invalid or metaId = "" then return invalid
        orderedEpisodeIds = packet.orderedVideoIds
        if orderedEpisodeIds = invalid or Type(orderedEpisodeIds) <> "roArray" or orderedEpisodeIds.Count() = 0 then return invalid
        if now = "" then now = m.time.NowIso()
        set = m.WatchedSetFor(metaId, orderedEpisodeIds)
        lastVideoId = m.LastWatchedId(set, orderedEpisodeIds, packet.videoId)
        bitfield = ""
        if m.codec <> invalid then bitfield = m.codec.WatchedEncode(orderedEpisodeIds, set, lastVideoId)
        item = m.stremioCodec.BuildWatchedItem(m.sessionType, m.stremioLibrary, now, packet, bitfield, lastVideoId)
        m.CommitStremioItem(item)
        return item
    end function

    ' The single commit every account write funnels through: the built item
    ' replaces the cached copy with the same _id (or is appended when the account
    ' library had never seen it). stremio-core keeps its local bucket current
    ' this way in update_and_push_items_to_storage, and it is what makes the
    ' write-back correct across push types — each build starts from what the last
    ' commit left, so a position write cannot revert a watched mark, or vice
    ' versa. A refused write (guest session, invalid packet) builds invalid and
    ' commits nothing.
    sub CommitStremioItem(item as dynamic)
        if item = invalid or item._id = invalid or item._id = "" then return
        if m.stremioLibrary = invalid then m.stremioLibrary = []
        for i = 0 to m.stremioLibrary.Count() - 1
            cached = m.stremioLibrary[i]
            if cached <> invalid and Type(cached) = "roAssociativeArray" and cached._id = item._id
                m.stremioLibrary[i] = item
                return
            end if
        end for
        m.stremioLibrary.Push(item)
    end sub

    ' Guest/stremio sessions persist under different keys so one session can
    ' never surface the other's saved content or continue-watching positions.
    function RegistryKey() as string
        if m.sessionType = "stremio"
            if m.accountScope <> "" then return "account_" + m.accountScope + "_library"
            return "stremio_library"
        end if
        return "library"
    end function

    ' Repoint the store at another session's data. A same-session switch is a
    ' no-op; everything is reloaded fresh so the in-memory state always mirrors
    ' the active session's persisted key.
    sub SwitchSession(sessionType as string, accountScope = invalid as dynamic)
        if sessionType <> "guest" and sessionType <> "stremio" then return
        nextScope = m.accountScope
        if GetInterface(accountScope,"ifString") <> invalid then nextScope = accountScope
        if sessionType = "guest" then nextScope = ""
        if m.sessionType = sessionType and m.accountScope = nextScope then return
        if m.registry <> invalid and m.sessionType = "stremio" and m.accountScope <> ""
            m.registry.Delete(m.RegistryKey())
            m.registry.Flush()
        end if
        m.accountScope = nextScope
        m.dirty = false
        m.registry = m.persistenceRegistry
        if sessionType = "stremio" and accountScope = "" then m.registry = invalid
        m.sessionType = sessionType
        m.saved = {}
        m.savedOrder = []
        m.positions = []
        m.stremioLibrary = []
        m.accountOutbox = []
        m.watched = {}
        m.accountWatched = {}
        m.unwatched = {}
        m.Load()
    end sub

    function MetadataKeyFor(metaId as string) as string
        if m.HasKey(m.saved,metaId)
            key = m.SafeProviderKey(m.saved[metaId].metadataProviderKey)
            if key <> "" then return key
        end if
        for each entry in m.positions
            if entry.metaId = metaId
                key = m.SafeProviderKey(entry.metadataProviderKey)
                if key <> "" then return key
            end if
        end for
        return ""
    end function

    function SafeProviderKey(value as dynamic) as string
        if GetInterface(value,"ifString") = invalid then return ""
        if not CreateObject("roRegex","^[0-9a-f]{64}$", "").IsMatch(value) then return ""
        return value
    end function

    function Save() as boolean
        m.dirty = true
        if m.registry = invalid then return false
        data = { continueWatching: m.positions }
        if m.sessionType = "stremio"
            data.accountOutbox = m.accountOutbox
            if m.accountOutbox.Count() > 0
                data.localWatched = m.watched
                data.localUnwatched = m.unwatched
            end if
        end if
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            data.saved = m.saved
            data.savedOrder = m.savedOrder
            data.watched = m.watched
        end if
        written = m.registry.Write(m.RegistryKey(), FormatJson(data)) = true
        committed = m.registry.Flush() = true
        m.dirty = not (written and committed)
        return not m.dirty
    end function

    function GetAccountOutbox() as object
        return m.accountOutbox
    end function

    function SetAccountOutbox(jobs as object) as boolean
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio" or Type(jobs) <> "roArray" or jobs.Count() > 128 then return false
        m.accountOutbox = jobs
        return m.Save()
    end function

    function SaveFailed() as boolean
        return m.dirty
    end function

    sub Load()
        if m.registry = invalid then return
        raw = m.registry.Read(m.RegistryKey())
        if raw = "" then return
        parsed = invalid
        try
            parsed = ParseJson(raw)
        catch e
            return
        end try
        if Type(parsed) <> "roAssociativeArray" then return
        if m.sessionType = "stremio" and Type(parsed.accountOutbox) = "roArray" and parsed.accountOutbox.Count() <= 128 then m.accountOutbox = parsed.accountOutbox
        if m.sessionType = "stremio" and m.accountOutbox.Count() > 0
            if Type(parsed.localWatched) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.watched = parsed.localWatched
            if Type(parsed.localUnwatched) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.unwatched = parsed.localUnwatched
        end if
        if m.sessionType <> "stremio"
            if parsed.saved <> invalid and Type(parsed.saved) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.saved = parsed.saved
            if parsed.savedOrder <> invalid and Type(parsed.savedOrder) = "roArray" then m.savedOrder = parsed.savedOrder
            if parsed.watched <> invalid and Type(parsed.watched) = "roAssociativeArray" then m.watched = parsed.watched
        end if
        if parsed.continueWatching <> invalid and Type(parsed.continueWatching) = "roArray" then m.positions = parsed.continueWatching
    end sub
end class
